jobs.description:
Are you looking for an active job with lots of variety? At FedEx in Duiven, you will contribute to a global logistics process. Your efforts ensure that packages reach their destination on time. In return, you will receive an attractive salary of €15.01 per hour, with shift allowances up to €19.51. Both 32-hour and 40-hour workweeks are possible.

What are you going to do?
In this dynamic role, you ensure that everything runs smoothly in the sorting process. Your tasks include:

- Sorting and processing incoming parcels;
- Transporting packages using a forklift;
- Efficiently loading parcels into trucks;
- Collaborating with colleagues to meet deadlines.
- You will work in the following shifts:

14:30 – 23:00

17:30 – 01:00

23:00 – 07:00

What do we offer?
- Gross hourly wage of €15.01, with allowances up to €19.51 per hour;
- Prospect of a permanent contract with FedEx;
- 8% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days;
- Travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometer;
- Pension accrual via Adecco from the age of 18;
- Access to the Adecco Academy for training and courses;
- A pleasant, safe working environment with supportive colleagues.

Where will you work?
FedEx is one of the largest logistics service providers in the world and ships millions of parcels daily from Duiven to more than 200 countries. Working safely, collaborating, and continuous growth are central values. Your contribution is seen and appreciated.

What do we ask?
- You speak Dutch and/or English;
- You are able to apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG) (costs will be reimbursed);
- You have your own transportation to Duiven;
- You have experience operating a forklift or are willing to learn;
- You are flexible and available for different shifts.

Are you interested?
Ready to get started? Click the apply button before September 26 , 2026 and take the next step in your career!

Questions? Call or WhatsApp Sanne at 06 42806892.

For our client in Kessel, we are looking for a production employee for the Maintenance and Laundry department. In this role, you’ll be responsible for inspecting used materials for quality, cleaning them, packaging, and getting them ready for transport or storage. You'll work with modern machinery to ensure the customer receives rental items that are complete, clean, and undamaged. You’ll be handling various tent components such as floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases, cleaning them both manually and with machines. Familiarity with industrial machinery and using a high-pressure cleaner is essential.

Your tasks will include:

- Washing and maintaining tent components and rental materials (e.g., floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases) by machine and hand;
- Operating industrial washers, dryers, high-pressure cleaners, and overhead cranes;
- Monitoring product quality and detecting any damages;
- Inspecting and packing canvases;
- Preparing materials for storage or transport;
- Maintaining a safe and sustainable workspace.

You will be working in an international environment where Dutch and English are the primary languages. Working hours are from 07:00 to 15:30, Monday through Friday.

We are seeking someone with experience in an industrial production setting and a hands-on approach. You’re not afraid to roll up your sleeves and tackle physical tasks. Additionally, you possess:

- A completed VMBO or basic vocational education (level 2) or an equivalent qualification;
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- A forklift certification, or you’re willing to obtain one;
- A desire to grow by participating in internal training opportunities.
